    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d94">

                <pb facs="0102" n="92" xml:id="pg92"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/9–2349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-09-23T16:00:00+08:00">September 23,
                            1949—4 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 24—10:43 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>779. Radio reports during past few days give much publicity to statements British
                    Government intends recognize Communist Government as soon as set up. American
                    business men here anxious learn whether US Government proposes similar action in
                    order determine their course action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
